Slices of one quantity in an order that the height lookup must not depend on:
an unnamed vertical slice through x = y = 0 first, then unnamed horizontal
slices from top to bottom. The smoke layer makes K grow with height, so a
wrong slice gives a different extinction coefficient.

&HEAD CHID='slice_order' /
&MESH IJK=16,16,12, XB=-2.0,2.0,-2.0,2.0,0.0,3.0 /
&TIME T_END=20.0 /
&DUMP NFRAMES=4, SMOKE3D=.FALSE. /
&REAC FUEL='PROPANE', SOOT_YIELD=0.1 /
&SURF ID='BURNER', HRRPUA=1000.0 /
&OBST XB=1.0,1.5,1.0,1.5,0.0,0.25, SURF_IDS='BURNER','INERT','INERT' /

&SLCF PBY=0.0, QUANTITY='EXTINCTION COEFFICIENT' /
&SLCF PBZ=2.5, QUANTITY='EXTINCTION COEFFICIENT', CELL_CENTERED=T /
&SLCF PBZ=1.5, QUANTITY='EXTINCTION COEFFICIENT', CELL_CENTERED=T /
&SLCF PBZ=0.5, QUANTITY='EXTINCTION COEFFICIENT', CELL_CENTERED=T /

&TAIL /
